{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>Me'od me'od.</b> Sometimes [it means] there is no more beyond it. And likewise, after he said \"and they covered all the high mountains,\" why did he say \"the mountains were covered\"? And so its meaning: every high mountain was covered with water, and fifteen cubits covered the aforementioned mountains. And we will believe the words of our Elohim, and we will abandon the vanities of human beings who say of a high mountain that it is in the kingdom of Yavan [Greece]."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {0 "Ibn Ezra objects to allegorical interpretations that identify the 'high mountains' with the Greek kingdom; he insists on the literal reading."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:43:40.561170415Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}